    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This study analyzes differences between the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) and the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development’s (OECD) global scripts and how they influence Sweden’s refugee education reform. Through qualitatively ascertaining the human rights-based policies as emphasized in the UNHCR’s Refugee Education 2030: A Strategy for Refugee Inclusion (2023), and the human capital-based policies as emphasized by the OECD’s Strength Through Diversity’s Spotlight Report for Sweden (2019), I compare the recommended policies to the official enacted policies that are present in the Swedish Ministry of Education’s legal educational framework, the School Act. I argue that tensions between human rights and human capital in Sweden’s refugee education reform are exacerbated by global pressures, supporting neo-institutional theory. Findings demonstrate the degree of each international governmental organization’s alignment in the Swedish refugee education reform, and contribute to the literature on refugee education, both globally and in Sweden.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Steel, M. (2024). Human Rights and Human Capital: The Influence of the UNHCR and the OECD on the Swedish Refugee Education Reform. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/hc754hh2792. https://doi.org/10.25740/hc754hh2792.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
